## Findings
1. advisory — brief:110 The Input domain omits two new readers that fail closed: `w341.test.ts` reads/imports owned source and package records, and `states.spec.ts` calls the reused `startServed` harness. Replace brief:110 with its current row followed by `| 9. Policy-row source, module and package inputs | owned sources/modules are readable/importable; package.json and package-lock.json are parseable and carry the asserted keys | read/load return empty sentinels and assertions fail; JSON parse or key mismatches fail node:test |` and `| 10. startServed(...) | resolves only after the reused harness obtains a port, token and 200 readiness response | startServed and waitForReady reject on spawn, early-exit, timeout or readiness failure, failing the Playwright test |`. [severity: S4] [class: spec×input-without-named-rejector] — check: apps/web/test/w341.test.ts
2. advisory — brief:106 Row 4 omits the Officina readers and falsely says every rejection becomes an error: `fetchActa` deliberately degrades, while the served Officina error row exercises `fetchHealth`. Replace brief:106 with `| 4. Screen read outcomes | Inbox fetchInbox; Seats fetchOfficina; Board reconciliation fetchOfficina/fetchOpera/fetchInbox; Officina fetchAerarium/fetchHealth/fetchCompletion are error-bearing. Each accepts the unchanged server route’s HTTP-200 JSON and rejects non-200, network or unparseable JSON; Officina fetchActa rejection remains an unchanged empty-strip degrade and stated limit. | getJSON rejects; Inbox/Seats reload, Board fetchBoardOnly/fullReconcile, and Officina’s three per-fetch catches convert rejection to the error state; the served 500 rows pin each screen |`. [severity: S2] [class: spec×input-domain-missing-or-unenforceable] — check: apps/web/tests-serve/states.spec.ts
3. advisory — brief:77 The 28 matrix cells are not the only reported states: every screen also reports `READY`, and `App` initializes it directly. Replace brief:77 with `Promise one-matrix: the seven matrix states are the only non-rest states the four screens report; at rest screenStatus reports READY, and every non-rest report is chosen by its one precedence — limit: the matrix covers the four live screens only; a future screen joins it by its own brief, and no check rule yet requires a kind: ui brief to carry these rows.` [severity: S2] [class: spec×prose-contradiction-under-revision] — check: apps/web/test/w341.test.ts
4. advisory — brief:81 A failed post-write reload leaves the last successful Inbox data in state, so the error can appear beside petition rows; only the initial failed read guarantees no rows. Replace brief:81 with `Promise no-invented-petitions: an initial failed Inbox read shows the error state with no petition rows and never substitutes demo petitions; a later reload failure reports error without inventing rows and may retain the last successful rows — limit: the ?demo=1 path still shows its demo petitions by design, and W-345 owns the Inbox’s other truth and safety items.` [severity: S2] [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: apps/web/tests-serve/states.spec.ts
5. advisory — brief:83 Several served cells do not visibly show their matrix copy: Seats pending shows a disabled Confirm, and Board/Officina use their existing visible copy while only the live region receives the matrix text. Replace brief:83 with `Promise served-cells-axe-clean: every served cell, at 1280 and at 390 except the two PHONE_UNREACHABLE cells, reaches the visible outcome named in the UI acceptance rows, announces its matrix copy, and has no axe-core 4.14.0 violation outside AXE_DISABLED_RULES — limit: color-contrast is disabled until W-361, axe’s automated rules are not full WCAG conformance, and only the steered states are scanned.` [severity: S2] [class: spec×promise-unattainable-under-accepted-domain] — check: apps/web/tests-serve/states.spec.ts
